---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { AUTHOR } from "../../../consts";

const description =
  "Privacy notice for Federico Di Luca's website: no data collected, no cookies, no tracking.";

const updated = "11 September 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description={description} locale="en">
  <section class="section page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="section-title">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="section-lead">
        The short version: this site collects no personal data, sets no cookies and does not track
        its visitors. Details below.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow privacy-body">
      <h2>Data controller</h2>
      <p>
        {AUTHOR.name}, {AUTHOR.city}, Italy. For any question about this notice or your data:
        <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}>{AUTHOR.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site collects</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. There are no forms, no traffic analytics, no tracking pixels and no social
        buttons talking to third parties. Every asset (images, icons, scripts) is served from this
        very domain: your browser contacts no other server to display these pages.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and preferences</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies. The only stored information is your light/dark theme choice,
        kept in your browser's <em>localStorage</em>: it stays on your device, is never
        transmitted, and you can clear it anytime from your browser settings. It is a purely
        technical preference, for which no consent is required.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub, Inc.). Like any hosting
        provider, GitHub may log visitors' IP addresses for security purposes and to comply with
        legal obligations, under the
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>If you write to me</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose to email me, your address and message land in my inbox and I use them solely
        to reply. I share them with no one and keep them only as long as needed to handle the
        conversation or any resulting collaboration. The legal basis is taking steps at your request
        prior to entering into a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to external services (LinkedIn, GitHub, MDPI, the Vocabe app). They are
        plain links: no data is exchanged until you open them. Once there, their own policies apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may request access to, rectification or erasure of your data (for this site, in
        practice, only any emails you sent me) and lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.
        To exercise them, write to the address above.
      </p>

      <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .privacy-body h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .privacy-body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .privacy-body p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .privacy-updated {
    margin-top: 2.5rem !important;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
</style>
